To find the value of $\greenD{x}$, divide both sides of the equation by $3$:

$\begin{align}
\blueD{\dfrac{\maroonD{15}}{3}}&=\blueD{\dfrac{\blueD{3}\greenD{x}}{3}} \\\\
\greenD{5} &= \greenD{x}
\end{align}$

To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\blueD{\text{multiply it by } 3} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{10}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD {y} &=\greenD{10} \blueD{\times 3} \\\\
\maroonD {y}&=\maroonD{30}
\end{align}$
